{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposal: ordinary staleness is never by itself a reason to re-ask a decision.\n\nWhen a request, promise or report is stale only because a basis under it was retired and succeeded — the reasoning moved, the requirements did not — the actor who authored it re-anchors it on the live successor and carries on. Nobody files a request asking whether the work is still wanted. Re-ask only when a condition of satisfaction changed, the addressee is no longer available, or the governing decision was itself retired without a successor. Evidence: second-application items 4–8 sat stale for nine days and then cost a human decision (request 1911873d, report a164296a) although the design note under them was unchanged at the same commit; the only thing that had moved was its artifact record. Adopt as discipline rule 11 in SKILL.md; planner implements on hugh's instruction.","body":{"adopts":"SKILL.md discipline rule: re-anchor stale-because-bases-moved requests on the live successor without re-asking; re-ask only on a changed condition, unavailable addressee, or a governing decision retired without successor"}}